    caiso_ps_plant_params: { cell: "K", ev: "ARMED IN THE KEEPER (2026-08-16-caiso-197-w2-r5, via the composed Wave-2 ladder; O -> K at the caiso-197 §6 promotion). caiso-197 lane 5 (results/calibration/FINDING-caiso197-ps-physical-2026-08-16.md; PRECHECK + build @ 56ddf497a pre-solve; records _caiso197_ps_citations.json + _caiso197_l5_gates.json) — U -> O 2026-08-16: ACCEPTED 6/6 on the pre-registered gates (GATESPEC-caiso195, owner ruling 7 GO WITH SCOPE RESTRICTIONS). Zero MW added (G-AGG exact 2,077.6 = 2,077.6); zones mechanical NP15 (G-ZONE); static cited bounds only, Hyatt in-block (G-NOSHAPE — caiso-141 §G untouched); ledger 11/8 unchanged, zero fitted scalars (G-DOF); engagement the campaign's largest (25.5k/33.1k/30.1k zone-hours re-priced, class-hour dispatch to 4.5 GW; pump caps bind at Helms 930<1053 and Gianelli 375.8<424). C3a moved ANTI-favorably (+4.4/+12.8/+15.9 vs control +4.4/+11.7/+14.5) and the arm is accepted anyway — the direction-hazard clause operating as written (rule 14; caiso-183 lineage). C3b worsens but passes all years (0.098/0.178/0.183 vs 0.20; 2025 margin 0.017 recorded as the composition watch). No pass->fail flip. Run 2026-08-16-caiso-197-l5-psphys (control shared). Citations: PG&E Helms deck (data/raw/reference/pge-helms-ps-plant-2008), DWR B132-22 tables (dwr-b132-22-swp-plants), USBR EWA EIS Ch.16; Eastwood pump/duration UNCITED -> disclosed unrestrained/incumbent defaults. Cell K follows the Wave-2 §6 C3a-blind promotion if the final composed rung survives" },
    measured_interface_limits: { cell: "K", ev: "caiso-51 (armed), caiso-132 (direction), caiso-133 (which limit), caiso-163 (internal N-S directional ratings; keeper); caiso-216 (Phase-0 witness: the armed S-to-N directional caps NEVER BIND for want of southern surplus — model south4 over the 5,400 MW Path-15 rating in only 17/234/289 h 2023/24/25 vs reality's 1,310/1,691/1,347 split hours, 0 h over path+storage; at the measured-membership what-if bound 342/742/1,143 h — the ratings are the price-formation machinery waiting on allocation; _caiso216_belly_surplus.json B2/B2b); caiso-220 (ALLOCATION LANDED ON THE SCORED PATH: with the measured membership crosswalk the armed S-to-N ratings now BIND on the solved P1 — NP15-SP15 > $15 in 50/40/17 h vs reality's 1310/1691/1347; the ratings engage in reality's direction, magnitude bounded by the caiso-218/219 strandedness nulls; FINDING-caiso220); caiso-218 (Phase-0 survey, decisive null: NO published internal-path operating-limit series exists 2023-25 — Path 15/26 TTC/ATC discontinued 2018-11-01, branch groups unenforced, live OASIS TI universe boundary-only, constraint reports shadow-price-only; DMM publishes the corridor's ELEMENT census with 2023 avg binding limits 200-2,500 MW — reality binds element-by-element far below the 5,400 aggregate; and the committed exceedance curves prove NO static single-link cap reproduces reality's non-monotone split vector [1,310/1,691/1,347] — the static-limit lever class is measured insufficient; _caiso218_limit_whatif.json, FINDING-caiso218 sect-B/C); caiso-219 (Phase-0 survey of the OTHER prerequisite - the sect-F.3a gen-pocket EXPORT limit - second decisive null: CAISO's sub-zonal deliverability record is censused complete (93 named constraints, Attachment A of the annual Transmission Capability Estimates, series 2019/2021/2023/2024) and every MW in it is ACCREDITATION HEADROOM for additional queued generation in a resource-weighted currency, NOT a flow rating - four independent misalignment axes, all stated by CAISO: currency (on-peak solar SCE 13%, PG&E 15% of nameplate; off-peak 77-79%; off-peak deliverability not performed at all in the 2024 TPD study), scope (OTC/existing deliverability deliberately not added back, so existing output + headroom is unrecoverable), nesting (Tehachapi sits behind 3 overlapping constraints at 6,149.1/6,733.2/1,333.6 MW FCDS), vintage (includes approved-but-unbuilt upgrades; an IRP forward planning input, not the as-operated 2023-25 grid). The TPD Allocation Reports publish only Overload % of an UNPUBLISHED rating (100-122% across every constraint table in the 2025 report); the ratings themselves are CEII. SUBSTANTIVE SIDE-RESULT: the same record's On-Peak/Off-Peak flag RE-LOCATES sect-F.3a - off-peak (belly-hour) binding is PG&E Fresno 14/19 and PG&E Kern 7/10, dominated by the GATES-MIDWAY complex (Path 15's southern terminus, ZP26 side), while Tehachapi is 0/3 off-peak and SCE Northern only 2/8 - independently corroborating caiso-218's element-not-cut conclusion and caiso-217's ZP26-below-SP15 zonal fact; _caiso219_deliverability_census.json, FINDING-caiso219 sect-C/D)" },
