    caiso_fsno_subzonal_topology: { cell: "R", ev: "caiso-224 (2026-08-30) — the static-DMM-cap arm FALSIFIED per the pre-registered §5 falsifiers, ADJUDICATED BY THE FINISHER SESSION from the committed artifacts (zero solves): F1 fires ALL THREE YEARS on NP15<->FSNO (binding share 0.3054/0.3547/0.3380 vs the 0.27 DMM ceiling — the rule-14 lower-bound parallel-path caps over-trap, largest exactly where the omitted-parallel set is largest) and F2 fires (arm split vector [1556/1359/1186] strictly year-ordered vs reality's non-monotone [1310/1691/1347] — single-vintage statics insufficient at sub-zonal grain, the caiso-218 §C signature). AND the structural thesis is CONFIRMED: north-south separation restored 52/40/14 h -> 1,556/1,359/1,186 h vs reality 1,310/1,691/1,347, negative-price mass migrating into the pocket (NP15 315/570/504 -> 98/121/175 neg h, FSNO 162/374/428); guards clean (C1 zero flips, C4 gas NRMSE improves all years, C8 forcing REDUCED 6.5/7.3/9.2% -> 5.3/5.6/6.6%); C3a lw -0.20/+0.22(wrong way)/-0.16 vs pre-bound -0.23/-0.32/-0.25, band-pass needs (-0.85/-1.90) not approached; C3b-2024 tripwire +0.015 named to the falsified caps. R is the CAPS, not the partition: the P-A' representation + caiso-223 membership + measured 3-way load split remain the standing sub-zonal representation; re-arm ONLY via W-2/W-3 (caiso-222 §(i)) or the F2-named backcast-admissible transmission-outage derate WATCH (unpublished today) as a data intake with its own precommit — never a re-tune of these caps (caiso-218 §F fences intact). Runs 2026-08-30-caiso-224-a0-control (G-CTRL BIT-ZERO, _caiso224_ctrl_tolerance.json) + 2026-08-30-caiso-224-b1-fsno; witness _caiso224_split_witness.json; PRECOMMIT-caiso224-fsno-arm-2026-08-30.md §5; FINDING-caiso224-fsno-arm-2026-08-30.md. caiso-230 (2026-09-01, zero solves) adds the STRUCTURAL reason no locational repricing can ever be a C3a instrument for CAISO: the C3a metric is the zone-hour load-weighted mean, so a mean-preserving zonal redistribution moves the dispersion without moving lambda by one cent (caiso-215's measured ISO-wide bridge terms of +/-$0.15 are the corroboration). And the model errs in the direction with no C3a value anyway: collapsed onto CAISO's own three trading hubs with the model's own demand weights and the SAME estimator on both sides, the model's zonal dispersion is 1.10/1.17/1.04 $/MWh against a measured DAM 5.57/4.67/3.31 and RTM 5.70/5.29/4.25 — the model UNDER-disperses by $2.3-4.6 in every year and both markets. This cell and the caiso-215 §F H4 strandedness object remain a legitimate C3b / D-A fidelity lane and are NEVER a C3a lane (FINDING-caiso230 §3, DO-NOT-REDO item 2)." },
